            <ArticleTitle>Identifying the causes of increased wound pain: the role of the tissue viability nurse.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>179-82</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A leg ulcer that had stopped healing was causing a patient increased pain. Heavy infection was identified as the cause, and found to be exacerbated by a range of factors. An assessment resulted in treatment changes, leading to complete healing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
